The chapter says guerrilla warfare uses small groups in a focused way, with speed, surprise and knowledge of the terrain. Show how the meeting with Afzal Khan at Pratapgad used:
(a) knowledge of the terrain;
(b) surprise;
(c) small groups against the enemy army.

Under the Sultans or the Mughals, an official often held a hereditary post and a land assignment. In Chhatrapati Shivaji's administration:
(a) what happened to hereditary posts;
(b) how was an official paid instead of through a land assignment;
(c) what else was done to many officials, and what did all these changes protect the king from?
